 "description": "C.2's staged fit redesigned (description, discarded seeds): a stage 1 that switches the network on,\nand fewer parameters (per-ligand tying), on benchmark v4's D_fit.\n\nThe plan review (`build/c2-fit-review-2026-11.md`, options B and C): stage 1 of the earlier staged\nfit never fitted the amphid sensory gains, so its network stayed silent, and stage 2's 196\ndimensions found bias-driven optima. Here, applied in this script (no package code changes):\n\n- the model: the encoded connectome under per-ligand modulator tying (132 parameters), with four\n  fitted pool centres (136);\n- the box: the three wiring scales on [0, 0.75] and every sensory gain on [-2, 2], each mapped onto\n  the encoder's unit box; every other range unchanged;\n- the readout: each output's pre-squash value through 2\u00b7tanh(x / 2), read as b + \u03a3_j w_j (pool_j - c_j);\n- the guard: a candidate whose motor layer saturates (over half its motor neurons at |h| > 0.99 in\n  over half the steps) scores 500 more;\n- stage 1: the 77 parameters that carry the senses to the outputs (the 7 wiring terms, the 36\n  sensory gains, the 25 readout weights and biases, the 5 noise terms, the 4 centres), every other\n  at the box centre; from the box centre, sigma0 0.2; CMA 9474; fit animals 708,000,000; the guarded\n  readiness stop or a cap of 200;\n- stage 2: all 136 from stage 1's answer, sigma0 0.1; CMA 9475; fit animals 710,000,000; run to 200.\n\nBoth stages: v4's ranking score on D_fit (with the guard), on the corrected wiring, 16 workers.\nEvery 50 generations, and at each stage's end, the answer is profiled (bounded pre-squash\npercentiles, primitive shares, time on the lawn, motor saturation, each food feature's gain onto\nthe pools; seed 99,670,000) and graded on D_fit's assays on one population (stage 1 at\n709,000,000, stage 2 at 711,000,000). Run from the repository root.\n",
